#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068370 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d1de6657-82b1-5bcb-b8cc-fd2629d31faa" :question/math-academy-id "e-10832" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' = \\dfrac {x^2}{y}.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}y^2 = \\dfrac{1}{3}x^3 + C.\n$$\n\nWe can express the solution in the form $y = y(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+2C \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+2C} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+K}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = 2C.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068371 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23d66cc8-8e5a-5a33-a7a1-c43f5facdcbc" :question/math-academy-id "e-10833" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' + 2xy = 0$ for $y\\neq 0.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+2xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln \\vert y \\vert = -x^2 + C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y = y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{x}^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = e^C$  and $K > 0.$ \n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ke^{-x^2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068372 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d908f1-591e-5cb6-afc5-fa7ec44ec326" :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32040154-373e-5a10-a460-1d17f6989da0" :question/math-academy-id "e-10849" :question/problem "Given that $x,y \\geq 0,$ separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\sqrt{2xy}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{g(y)} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} =  \\sqrt{2x} \\cdot  \\sqrt{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{y}} \\cdot \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} = \\sqrt{2x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068374 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d53c6172-978d-57c7-b1f0-e56e892e48a9" :question/math-academy-id "e-10997" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n    =\n    \\dfrac{x}{y}.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{y} \\\\ y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+2K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C= 2K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ny^2 = x^2 + C .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f82833d6-76e7-526f-8690-513b935ffc80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{2x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311392} {:answer/id #uuid "ab3e08a0-05d6-5f27-be05-eb7635d17b5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311393} {:answer/id #uuid "28ea0db4-a307-51b9-8d43-26c6d713de6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{2x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311394} {:answer/id #uuid "534e3799-1c4d-5051-a2f0-cee6bd143819" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311395} {:answer/id #uuid "08b86fa1-74c1-52ae-9d88-a7f80bc9f7e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=2{e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "534e3799-1c4d-5051-a2f0-cee6bd143819" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311395} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3226a4d-2e16-5c47-adc4-39cfe15f3aad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f6a01c34-9b8c-5742-a002-5656bbb5e9ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-118885" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}{cos}^{2}⁡y$ for $0<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}{cos}^{2}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡y & ={e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc7e6ed2-6dae-57e8-aa53-481d27d83d76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Ke^{-\\cos x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065711} {:answer/id #uuid "c598e2c1-a3d7-5672-9e1b-55f44ecf443a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{-\\sin x} + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065712} {:answer/id #uuid "1fffb016-acf6-5df4-bfc2-e923faa9914f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\cos x + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065713} {:answer/id #uuid "30d67981-c70b-5427-8b87-2c498032c7b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{-\\cos x} + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065714} {:answer/id #uuid "5d86bad1-df45-5a03-903c-5f7f277d995c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\ln \\cos x + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc7e6ed2-6dae-57e8-aa53-481d27d83d76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Ke^{-\\cos x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065711} :answer-field/id #uuid "134b4ace-23ce-5202-beb3-330b0514f916" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "432fe98f-ffaf-5033-958e-d3cb37de9f8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-14244" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311397 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2398db1-88c9-574c-91fa-70c569652e09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{3{x}^{2}+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311399} {:answer/id #uuid "5415f72f-9dd4-53d1-8dc6-09655c362101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311400} {:answer/id #uuid "3e44b657-91bd-589b-a1d1-611d26d8f603" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311401} {:answer/id #uuid "1c36ba58-cea6-5f95-bafc-9814cf59d93a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311402} {:answer/id #uuid "d22f4e71-4ecc-5851-886f-48f02106a8aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5415f72f-9dd4-53d1-8dc6-09655c362101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311400} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6725044-65b4-5d9c-9e33-f0f0efa45de9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "321b7d69-9883-59b2-a4d0-4ebf210bb530" :question/math-academy-id "q-14247" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y+3y{x}^{2}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y+3y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y+3y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(1+3{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1+3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =x+{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{3}+x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84379651-35ea-52b3-97fa-614e5ead0f20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{y^{3}}{3} + y + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065717} {:answer/id #uuid "bddcf8bf-dea4-577e-b7b0-741fb768f4e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\sec (x) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065718} {:answer/id #uuid "f184319f-a95e-5e73-a5b6-9827d78020db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\tan (x + C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065719} {:answer/id #uuid "2fe5eeee-833f-53b7-8b83-0a6fe948aa64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\tan (x + 1) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065720} {:answer/id #uuid "3463cd70-9638-5db9-9bdd-a3b32a75b6d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\cot (x + C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f184319f-a95e-5e73-a5b6-9827d78020db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\tan (x + C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065719} :answer-field/id #uuid "07f31081-c281-5658-b7ef-4581c11a6aee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c17c4aa5-1ffc-5c4e-9267-85cce391b502" :question/math-academy-id "q-14257" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}={y}^{2}+1.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={y}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y) & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y)=x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03daf3fe-5900-5737-94b7-8be50d710f85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311406} {:answer/id #uuid "2d194fc1-1b54-547d-811f-8c77414c1ee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311407} {:answer/id #uuid "030e2cbd-9d58-5290-b1d9-91417538f250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311408} {:answer/id #uuid "ec29e029-fed1-5d53-a9e3-813ab000e0f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311409} {:answer/id #uuid "31493b54-06f9-5e3e-9f8e-15343c3c84f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "030e2cbd-9d58-5290-b1d9-91417538f250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311408} :answer-field/id #uuid "52ecedda-ee36-5ee3-93e0-3e3fb3da0ef2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fed70404-5aaf-52d2-8686-4c656a529df4" :question/math-academy-id "q-154357" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡y}$ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡y} \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡y & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a406919-2533-5bf3-87e6-cd3122ff57cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{y} = x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065813} {:answer/id #uuid "af89d087-1bce-5d10-b727-77195253adf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}e^{2y} = x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065814} {:answer/id #uuid "eb82afe8-e01f-578c-bbde-72a44be6e6da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{y} = x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065815} {:answer/id #uuid "3212ed8a-aa8b-5826-9b94-3081f493c231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e^{y} = x^{3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065816} {:answer/id #uuid "66d39395-7c92-5a4a-97ca-0e22e39188ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}e^{2y} = 2x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a406919-2533-5bf3-87e6-cd3122ff57cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{y} = x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065813} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6a47be1-a211-5316-bdf4-302ab41ba393" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8653163f-c134-5fe5-8ca8-a073f08d08b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-154359" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{e}^{y}}.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{{e}^{y}} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ed89cd4-db12-5c49-ae2a-17aea3d08188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}=\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290022} {:answer/id #uuid "56616332-794d-51ea-af06-084f11a43f74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290023} {:answer/id #uuid "deb58696-83e2-5555-817f-215602279b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290024} {:answer/id #uuid "1189f080-3a6e-5660-afd7-8cc50119a3d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290025} {:answer/id #uuid "48746e41-b515-521b-a7e0-237e5b4d84ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1189f080-3a6e-5660-afd7-8cc50119a3d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290025} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ab8e971-cfb0-51b3-b12f-7a645d1412c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a72cd73-068f-5aa7-91b3-dbc11c176b22" :question/math-academy-id "q-154373" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2{y}^{3/2}}{3} & =\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+K \\\\ {y}^{3/2} & ={x}^{3/2}+C \\\\ \\sqrt{{y}^{3}} & =\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{3K}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d908f1-591e-5cb6-afc5-fa7ec44ec326" :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9372fe8a-9fe7-5b4d-bda4-372a083ddca5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x + 1}{x} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = y^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065831} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f4abee-366d-5610-8fb5-d09a162b2c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{y^{2}}{x + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065832} {:answer/id #uuid "f7f10af7-a270-5ce4-a424-4307343938cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 1) \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = xy^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065833} {:answer/id #uuid "714ca07c-83ac-5ede-be6f-c4ae92b77715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{2} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{x}{x + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065834} {:answer/id #uuid "75b0eb6d-0154-58d2-9a2d-8276d5ffdc36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y^{2}} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{x}{x + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75b0eb6d-0154-58d2-9a2d-8276d5ffdc36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y^{2}} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{x}{x + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065835} :answer-field/id #uuid "65e4bc99-ff97-5d84-85c3-18160f4ad8ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8143064d-a592-5c44-b653-c218df46c5ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-154678" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{x+1}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(\\frac{x}{x+1})\\cdot {y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+1}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d908f1-591e-5cb6-afc5-fa7ec44ec326" :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "923d0c10-516e-522c-af35-b4848335d4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-y} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065849} {:answer/id #uuid "bcce1e70-26c0-5859-b057-fab6c48f781a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-x} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065850} {:answer/id #uuid "e115c657-7686-534b-8084-d76a998bb3ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{y} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065851} {:answer/id #uuid "24dc42fe-bafe-5fea-98d3-b1147bb4f023" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = e^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065852} {:answer/id #uuid "6dcc00ac-7620-515a-82e8-693fd76a876e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-x} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = e^{-y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "923d0c10-516e-522c-af35-b4848335d4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-y} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} = e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065849} :answer-field/id #uuid "483dc0ad-506e-5219-8731-d4f7720ce3bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ed05f1b-222f-5d8f-b307-8248e81b3d7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-157692" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x+y}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{y}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{e}^{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x},\n$$\n\nor, equivalently,\n\n$$\n{e}^{-y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290041 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1f8f621-d93c-502b-8675-9db1faf29bd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290043} {:answer/id #uuid "602ddebc-9875-542b-bfb3-35cd8e105d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290044} {:answer/id #uuid "0af79cfa-50c7-5ccc-a34a-b105fb640511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290045} {:answer/id #uuid "ebde7d7b-7708-5f47-93ea-fb66358a313d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290046} {:answer/id #uuid "fa647dc1-91e8-5f0d-b7b8-bea8690818ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0af79cfa-50c7-5ccc-a34a-b105fb640511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290045} :answer-field/id #uuid "92306383-ac9e-5217-8c24-3963a5997891" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0b2f5622-0ea4-5d24-ae30-e39b34ff5b26" :question/math-academy-id "q-158013" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89cb340f-0478-584c-b2ef-13f05abef887" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311413} {:answer/id #uuid "34609bcf-9819-55ba-9ad6-58492df84acb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311414} {:answer/id #uuid "7c5bca59-1c2d-504d-ba7c-a8b66a6a82eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311415} {:answer/id #uuid "11a47ba4-f242-5f17-967a-c31ff9f17190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311416} {:answer/id #uuid "c03d2759-88bd-5b8a-885b-23c829ab9bdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c5bca59-1c2d-504d-ba7c-a8b66a6a82eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311415} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c763e14-0bd0-5572-8ef8-79991bf0d840" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac44d433-a7db-5b48-a5c5-fbb14f94435f" :question/math-academy-id "q-158017" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d908f1-591e-5cb6-afc5-fa7ec44ec326" :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c749822-94c7-5c64-8c64-4c6266ddfeb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{3}}{{2}^{x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311420} {:answer/id #uuid "564def48-6013-59e6-9baf-190b7104df0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311421} {:answer/id #uuid "38df9078-ba5c-5fad-b6cd-04e7a2c8eb0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311422} {:answer/id #uuid "5fe54718-6808-5e7a-a523-0f7ed9bb0994" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311423} {:answer/id #uuid "bb32a9d2-9e67-5063-ab6f-b3b6a29ddb6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb32a9d2-9e67-5063-ab6f-b3b6a29ddb6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311424} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d798e2d-0f06-548c-a16c-b2ee7dde6f1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba587f1b-dab3-553a-b4db-544d035b8b45" :question/math-academy-id "q-158025" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{y}^{3}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290076 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d908f1-591e-5cb6-afc5-fa7ec44ec326" :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200ff40b-c483-5511-ada4-9962f1c23d0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290078} {:answer/id #uuid "549aa129-3c38-5279-aaf0-8fc6677cb0c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290079} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6f447c-5fc8-5dfe-8140-683e78c870c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290080} {:answer/id #uuid "91acb97c-fd3b-5dfa-afb4-225be15bbf45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290081} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba46a08-ea30-56e0-baae-58f6e1ba67d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ba46a08-ea30-56e0-baae-58f6e1ba67d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290082} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ebceda-4b19-5c0e-a39b-5accbe931e11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb5bb3ab-6532-5577-9047-8f7af02e49c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-158026" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}{x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290083 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d908f1-591e-5cb6-afc5-fa7ec44ec326" :knowledge-point/title "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df758d0e-cfd9-5633-9937-06734f1dadad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290085} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5e4add-8474-56c5-b9f1-74138be46566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290086} {:answer/id #uuid "e1200b00-76c5-56c4-9805-fe8cd02cdea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290087} {:answer/id #uuid "250598c9-e4a7-528c-b6e1-4d20fc85fffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290088} {:answer/id #uuid "026d5bf6-a7c1-5e06-8422-0743ce837bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\text{ }\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad5e4add-8474-56c5-b9f1-74138be46566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290086} :answer-field/id #uuid "95e320e5-1eb4-517c-9bd9-97745a54c3a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1966b7ec-9eb0-519d-bc45-7210a4a3667d" :question/math-academy-id "q-158027" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot {y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Implicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bae4517-ca75-59cb-a32f-b2a2a2c2eaa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290092} {:answer/id #uuid "0aeecf5d-5702-513e-801c-5c126e01c8a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290093} {:answer/id #uuid "17ce1359-aa2a-5472-9c96-f2901f6cba5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{ }y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290094} {:answer/id #uuid "222d92b3-2dcd-5344-b8b0-8d766efd687a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290095} {:answer/id #uuid "201dba49-412a-5f39-a491-3eaaf266d447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "201dba49-412a-5f39-a491-3eaaf266d447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290096} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0239e82-ea6b-51fb-b67b-3105cf1e47e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "575d49f3-8bd3-5463-bab9-a94f8bc81fb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-158035" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y & ={x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311425 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "095c386d-e826-5ea2-a5fb-30f72af48e88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311427} {:answer/id #uuid "ad4aa770-c8f3-5ef3-8ef4-ac28d2806dd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311428} {:answer/id #uuid "f115aba7-d8f5-5d0b-8c18-05b7b59d2bc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{{x}^{2}}+{e}^{{x}^{3}}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311429} {:answer/id #uuid "bce41ee9-5b15-52f9-8585-7ad4ee731284" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{3}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311430} {:answer/id #uuid "810d8ae3-e659-552e-991f-6b14f26edca2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "095c386d-e826-5ea2-a5fb-30f72af48e88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311427} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d6f149e-7d48-587b-8cb2-9be31ecbf0be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c533f957-5ce4-560a-af3f-547368ddc163" :question/math-academy-id "q-3854" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(2x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Solution in Explicit Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ce0949a-0ea0-5360-adbf-f161a9ff3f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295232} {:answer/id #uuid "a387ccd1-f06b-5ffe-b783-cb8b81fbbe33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295233} {:answer/id #uuid "ac82fc84-dfaa-51f4-b138-ae94c4b491b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{6x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295234} {:answer/id #uuid "d280d431-b9b1-558d-accc-d726f6290102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295235} {:answer/id #uuid "6642f64e-99b2-5e95-9f2a-31c65e5a51e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(6x+C)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d280d431-b9b1-558d-accc-d726f6290102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295235} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1296824-4d0d-5645-aae2-6b215316cc08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295231}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "52368e24-e78c-5f40-b95b-9857942b42f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-51256" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6x\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6x\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\cdot 3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\int {y}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{1/3} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/3}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311432 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b424038f-53ec-50b8-a577-28ac20132663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311434} {:answer/id #uuid "5146ed63-5fe6-5163-b942-ab4d2f76fc29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311435} {:answer/id #uuid "44ea5ccd-9db8-5f00-84c6-f669861f31ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311436} {:answer/id #uuid "b9049a8a-81ee-5b86-84bd-f48f3676fff2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311437} {:answer/id #uuid "3db25045-43dd-5a7d-b7f1-a13ee117b7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b424038f-53ec-50b8-a577-28ac20132663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311434} :answer-field/id #uuid "8797a9ff-99b0-5fd2-ac06-80813f3e4551" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d9f3f4e8-eb82-571e-bb8f-ae7778e94ec7" :question/math-academy-id "q-79666" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2y}=0$ for $y>0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2y} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2y} \\\\ 2y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2y\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88e43912-62f7-5a33-9a76-7f51fd9f31ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = (x^{2} + x)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068286} {:answer/id #uuid "b8596a92-ac9c-5b2a-850c-e7b27b6d6ad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = (\\frac{x^{2} + x + C}{2})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068287} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1b0f02-f762-564c-aa7f-2380417c7edf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = (\\frac{x^{2} + x}{2})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068288} {:answer/id #uuid "cf8e98ae-c8fc-584d-9fb4-b50ba813b1bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = x^{2} + x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068289} {:answer/id #uuid "f67e1534-03a7-5e27-9835-eeecccbddce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = (x^{2} + x + C)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8596a92-ac9c-5b2a-850c-e7b27b6d6ad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = (\\frac{x^{2} + x + C}{2})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068287} :answer-field/id #uuid "459788ea-078f-5030-8173-ec774f1d10ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "679701a5-b0c3-5865-adfd-e49e046da668" :question/math-academy-id "q-8303" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-\\sqrt{y}=2x\\sqrt{y}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{y} & ={x}^{2}+x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{y}={x}^{2}+x+C\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069460 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "873996aa-22f5-5b88-8e75-167e4b093cce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Ke^{\\sin x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068292} {:answer/id #uuid "9140f707-6730-50a1-804b-92b31cf5f648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Ke^{-\\cos x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068293} {:answer/id #uuid "c96b87cd-4495-5236-a386-797ada3b613d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Ke^{\\cos x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068294} {:answer/id #uuid "e2eed065-175a-5a55-a12b-c3d1cc73ee5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{\\sin x} + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068295} {:answer/id #uuid "4904ed99-1755-5150-b2c2-74ae268ebcb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = e^{-\\cos x} + K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "873996aa-22f5-5b88-8e75-167e4b093cce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Ke^{\\sin x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068292} :answer-field/id #uuid "3886366a-b91e-5dfb-a240-a1c3975d5795" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b946e806-cd3a-503b-8b7c-fe17b0906080" :question/math-academy-id "q-8305" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y=0$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$"}]}
